<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch company results due Oct 28.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch company results due Oct 28.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of Dutch company results for week beginning Monday, Oct 28 include:</p>
<p>DATE--COMPANY-------PERIOD--PFT/DIV--CONSENSUS--RANGE-----PVS</p>
<p> 29/10 DSM		Q3	 PFT    196.7    181-212     234</p>
<p> 31/10 Royal Dutch*   Q3	 PFT   1144.5   1025-1264   1053</p>
<p> 31/10 Royal Dutch+   Q3	 PFT   1215.3   1115-1330   1117</p>
<p> 31/10 KNP BT	   Q3	 PFT     38.9     33-48	116</p>
<p> 01/11 Atag	   9 months   PFT     15.9   15.3-16.6     15.9</p>
<p>and in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>* Royal Dutch net income forecast figure is in millions of Sterling.</p>
<p>+ Royal Dutch current cost net forecast figure also in millions of Sterling.</p>
<p>Securities houses surveyed included: Amstgeld, Bangert Pontier, BZW, Delta Lloyd Bank, Generale Bank, ING, Kempen &amp; Co, Labouchere, Lanschot Bankiers, Rabo/IRIS, Strating and Wesselius.</p>
<p>NOTE - Banks and brokers interested in contributing to Reuters surveys can contact the Amsterdam newsroom on +31-20-504-5000 or fax their forecasts to +31-20-504 5040.</p>
<p>For the week starting Nov 4 we are collecting Q3 result forecasts for Hunter Douglas, Akzo Nobel, Unilever and 1/2 YR 96/97 of KLM .</p>
<p>Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (FAX 31-20-504-5040)</p>
</text>
